    <p>Painting has always run on word of mouth, and a five-to-seven-year exterior that still looks sharp is the best advertising you own. But Hartselle is full of homeowners who research everything, and the newcomers among them have no one to ask. The family that relocated for the schools and wants the sun-faded exterior repainted right doesn't have a painter's name — they search, and compare, and read reviews before they call. The buyer who just took on an older home downtown with layered, failing paint is typing it into Google, not asking a neighbor they don't have yet. Those researchers never touch your referral chain, and reaching them is <a href="/articles/why-word-of-mouth-isnt-enough/">where word of mouth alone runs out</a> once a town grows faster than your best jobs can be seen. A real page, with the work photographed honestly, is the only thing that puts you in front of them.</p>

